## New finding (outside the baseline)

**Fingerprint (recommend filing, not fixing): `correct-path-unit-gate-unequal-between-equivalent-outcome-classes`**
severity low-medium / symptom: two answers with identical numeric correctness are scored `wrong` or `correct_other_form` depending only on period order / root cause: `checker.py:294` gates `correct` on `answer["unit"] == gold.target_unit`, while `correct_other_form` at `checker.py:282-287` has no unit conjunct / premises violated: spec §2 `correct` rule (`WP0_TATQA_ADAPTER_CHECKER_CONTRACT_v1.md:33`, "…row and periods match" — unit not mentioned) **and** the author's own `implementation_contract.md:74` rule 7 ("Both values correct -> `correct`") — the code diverges from both / also unrecorded in `deviations`, and untested: all 8 taxonomy answers use `"unit":"unit"`, and `normal_unit` has `target_unit: null`, so no fixture exercises correct-deltas-with-mismatched-unit / fix: either add the unit conjunct to `correct_other_form` **and** record the tightening as a deviation with a fixture case, or drop the conjunct from `correct` to match spec — never silently.

Secondary, spec-level only: leak-guard needles blind to `1,300` / `1.3e3` / `001300` renderings (§5(a) does not mandate them) — fingerprint `leak-guard-needle-blind-to-alternate-numeric-renderings`, hardening opportunity for the WP-2 freeze.

